# UTC. commerce times from contracts/entrypoints.md §스케줄, which now names all six -- every
# commerce Dataset member gets a line, per S05 (playbook 02-test-discipline.md T10 records a real
# outage from a dataset with a collector and no cron line). Spacing here is a gap rule, not a minute
# rule: each line's gap to the next has to cover how long it runs, which is its sources' min_interval_s
# times how many requests they make. No runtime is written down here -- the test computes it from those
# policy constants so it follows them (contracts/entrypoints.md §스케줄).
0 * * * *   cosmai collect commerce --dataset ranking
5 2 * * *   cosmai collect commerce --dataset product
30 3 * * *  cosmai collect commerce --dataset review_low --board suncare
15 4 * * *  cosmai collect commerce --dataset review
45 4 * * *  cosmai collect commerce --dataset review_stats
30 5 * * *  cosmai collect commerce --dataset new_product
# analyze all is DB-only (no external fetch), so contracts/entrypoints.md §스케줄 exempts it from the
# gap rule the commerce walks follow.
0 5 * * *   cosmai analyze all
# naver datalab: monthly (키워드 사전 기준, contracts/entrypoints.md), day 1. 06:10 clears every
# commerce time above (02:05/03:30/04:15/04:45/05:30); naver walks a different host, so the commerce
# gap rule does not bind it.
10 6 1 * *  cosmai collect naver --dataset datalab
# naver blog: monthly too -- every run re-walks all 15 keyword-group terms from scratch (no
# cursor; natural-key upsert on post_id makes that safe), so once a month is enough spend.
# 06:40 clears datalab (06:10), analyze all (05:00, entrypoints.md §스케줄) and every commerce time.
40 6 1 * *  cosmai collect naver --dataset blog
